Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 20:09:15 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Address ChatGPT's C4b/C4c review: test-galaxy guard, leash
 locking and routes, request ids

Findings from Documentation-support/review-C4b/C4b-C4c-review.md:

1 (P1) /agentgear and /agentskill now also require a disposable test galaxy:
  isDisposableTestGalaxy() (new SandboxTestGalaxy.h) is true only when the
  database name ends in "_test", which test_galaxy.py sets and live never uses
  (live has no DBName override, so it is "swgemu"). A copied Core3.AgentGear
  flag can no longer enable them on live.
2 (P1) The leash task cross-locks the leader (follower held, then leader: the
  engine's deadlock-safe pattern), so the group/planet/range checks, the route
  and the move all use one consistent view of both characters.
3 (P1) The leash only ever moves the follower along a navmesh route: to 3 m
  short of the leader when the route reaches them, otherwise to the route's
  reachable end. No route: no move. A move that gains nothing is skipped, with
  one message ("as close as the ground allows") instead of rubber-banding.
4 (P2) /agentpath takes an optional "id:<n>" first token and echoes it; the
  agent body sends a fresh id per request and matches on it, so a late reply
  for the same destination is ignored.
5 (P2) The group-member menu says "Stop leash" only on the current leader; on
  anyone else it says "Leash to this member instead", which is what it does.
6 (P2) The body clears its mission cache on a scene change, and forgets a
  mission (and its radial menu) on destroy even after its scene was dropped.
7 (P2) A mission baseline replaces the record; a waypoint field without an id
  or coordinates removes the old waypoint.

Tested on the test galaxy (bot squads, 13 Oct 20:20): leash 2.1 m from the leader with no repeated
hops, menu labels right in a three-person group, paths with request ids (Esk 5/5), gear and training
still granted on the test galaxy. Not exercised: planet change mid-leash, disconnected terrain,
mission cache after zoning (no mission terminal found yet).

Agent: Claude
